  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "CUP-01",
      "title": "The finite chart labels and determinant correction",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-cusp-cover",
      "statement": "For every totally complex L and N≥1 a fixed finite list of rational-up-to-placewise-scalar translates of one Siegel region meets every SL_N(𝒪_L)-orbit in the product of complex SL_N groups.",
      "hypotheses": "Adelic reduction into a compact triangular factor, positive common diagonal and maximal compact subgroup; compactness of its finite projection, openness of integral finite GL, recovery of integral entries of a rational matrix from all finite integrality conditions, finite generation of the number-field units and N≥1.",
      "definitions": [
        "The finite-part map sends a rational matrix to its components at all finite places. Two rational matrices in the same left coset of integral finite GL differ, on the left by the inverse of the chosen representative, by an integral invertible matrix.",
        "D(u)=diag(u,1,…,1), det δ=v^N u₀ with u₀ in the list built from torsion and reduced unit exponents.",
        "The finite labels are (g,u₀) with g drawn from the inverse GL representative list. At w, the translate is z_w w(D(u₀⁻¹)g) of determinant one."
      ],
