      "id": "CUP-03",
      "title": "A finite cover bounds the quotient integral",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-cusp-integral",
      "statement": "For a nonnegative Γ-invariant f, an arithmetic Haar fundamental domain F and the selected translates, ∫_F f ≤ ∑ⱼ∫_S f(cⱼy). For the height moment of order A each summand is finite if N≥A+2.",
      "hypotheses": "Countable discrete arithmetic group; left-invariant Haar measure; the finite translates meet every arithmetic orbit; the normalized height is Γ-invariant; chartwise exponential height bound and single-region integrability with 2A<2(N−1).",
